<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philippine Organic Act (1902)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1902</span> · Also known as Philippine Bill of 1902, Cooper Act</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Philippine Organic Act of 1902 was the first basic law for the civil government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. It confirmed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-commission">Philippine Commission</a>, extended a bill of rights to Filipinos, and provided for an elected Philippine Assembly once peace and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/census">census</a> were achieved; the assembly first met in 1907. It also dealt with the friar lands and natural resources.</p></div>
